# Coding-file extensions that Finder opens with Code Root.app (VS Code at the
# file's git root). One per line; scripts/setup-code-root.sh reads this file
# for both the app's document claims and the LaunchServices defaults.
#
# Left alone on purpose:
#   plist        often binary, which VS Code can't display; Xcode can
#   html, htm    the double-click intent is viewing it in the browser
#   ts           macOS types .ts as an MPEG-2 transport stream, so claiming it
#                would also claim video files
#   txt csv tsv log   text and data, not code

